# A scripted debugging session for fact.sa.
#
# The session always stops at the entry instruction first: that is where a
# script sets its breakpoints, before the program has run. After that, one
# command line is consumed per stop, so "step 3" is followed by whatever the
# script wants read at the instruction it stopped on.
#
# 0x0001c8 is the source offset prog.ir prints for the recursive call inside
# fact (`; source-offset 0001c8 -> I102`).
break src 0x0001c8
run
where
bt
info
step 3
where
reg SP
delete 89
info
break 89
continue
